##
    How Books phrases things, which is nobody else's business.

    No visibility is written, so this reaches its own project and stops there.
    Library references Books and still cannot name Wording — which is the point. Books can
    change how it phrases a book, or delete this model outright, without breaking anyone,
    because nobody outside could have depended on it.

    Book is public for the opposite reason: Library is meant to use it, so it says so.
##

# @summary: How Books phrases a book, reachable only inside Books.
model Wording

    # @summary: Joins a title and an author into one readable line.
    # @title: what the book is called.
    # @author: who wrote it.
    # @yields: the two joined with "by".
    public global string function Join(string title, string author)
        yield title + " by " + author;
    end function

end model
